From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:27:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Power down the unused
 ISP

Nothing on J713 uses the ISP yet, but it is left powered at boot.
Enable the ISP_SYS domain in the board policy so that genpd turns it off
as an unused domain; a future camera driver will power it up through the
normal path.

On battery with the display blanked, powering ISP_SYS off lowers the
3.8 V rail by about 65 mW (three off/on pairs: +69, +61, +65 mW). The
domain stays off across s2idle and the display is unaffected.

The T8132 platform handoff builds its embedded J713 policy from this
file and disables any PMGR domain the policy does not list, so the
kernel and DTB must come from the same tree for this to take effect.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit ea08c2aaa246511de6afa3ab5506927b00277caa)
[dylan: J604 form of the J713 change: the same &ps_isp_sys enable in
 t8132-j604-pmgr.dtsi, which takes the J713 decision for every domain no
 J604 node consumes. ISP_SYS is the SoC-level node of 50d89e75eb
 (t8132-pmgr.dtsi, PMGR offset 0x530); no J604 node consumes it. The
 J604 power saving is not measured yet.]
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 94238b578558661f5ef53503755cb794aceb52da)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi
index a478286000..284fd06433 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi
@@ -404,6 +404,11 @@ &ps_isp_sys {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* No camera driver yet; genpd powers the ISP down as an unused domain. */
+&ps_isp_sys {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &ps_ans {
 	status = "okay";
 };
